{"tool_name":"titindb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"TITINdb","home":"http://fraternalilab.kcl.ac.uk/TITINdb/","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Computational tool to assess titin\u2019s role as a disease gene.","addition_date":"2019-07-07T13:47:41Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:08:19.618574Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:TITINdb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"franca.fraternali@kcl.ac.uk","name":"Franca Fraternali","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"http://fraternalilab.kcl.ac.uk/TITINdb/tutorials/"},{"type":["General"],"url":"http://fraternalilab.kcl.ac.uk/TITINdb/documentation/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"},{"term":"Variant classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3225"},{"term":"Variant prioritisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3226"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"TITINdb","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx424","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: Large numbers of rare and unique titin missense variants have been discovered in both healthy and disease cohorts, thus the correct classification of variants as pathogenic or non-pathogenic has become imperative. Due to titin's large size (363 coding exons), current web applications are unable to map titin variants to domain structures. Here, we present a web application, TITINdb, which integrates titin structure, variant, sequence and isoform information, along with pre-computed predictions of the impact of non-synonymous single nucleotide variants, to facilitate the correct classification of titin variants. Availability and implementation: TITINdb can be freely accessed at http://fraternalilab.kcl.ac.uk/TITINdb. Contact: franca.fraternali@kcl.ac.uk. Supplementary information: Supplementary data are available at Bioinformatics online.","authors":[{"name":"Fraternali F."},{"name":"Gautel M."},{"name":"Laddach A."}],"citationCount":32,"date":"2017-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics (Oxford, England)","title":"TITINdb-a computational tool to assess titin's role as a disease gene"},"pmcid":"PMC5860166","pmid":"29077808","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"NMR","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0593"},{"term":"Pathology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0634"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"TITINdb","home":"https://bio.tools/TITINdb","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Computational tool to assess titin\u2019s role as a disease gene.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:titindb/web/fraternalilab.kcl.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"training_material":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":27,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":2,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2024"},{"count":3,"year":"2025"},{"count":4,"year":"2020"},{"count":4,"year":"2023"},{"count":6,"year":"2019"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx424","pmcid":"PMC5860166","pmid":"29077808","ref_count":22,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2006"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2015"},{"count":3,"year":"2013"},{"count":4,"year":"2014"},{"count":6,"year":"2016"}],"title":"TITINdb-a computational tool to assess titin's role as a disea